  "commits": [
    {
      "sha": "c3f507391487cb56813b5bdc9e6354a8e4a0ddda",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/c3f507391487cb56813b5bdc9e6354a8e4a0ddda",
      "message": "Document how to run the blueprint fixture writers without racing\n\nTwo raw writer runs in one checkout share its default test database and fail on migrations. Say to run one at a time, prefer artifacts sync where the channel has a check, and why contrib test reports a changed watcher fixture as a failed run.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-10T01:40:54Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "81d5422e41326b7b34aac131553c9f531b057661",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/81d5422e41326b7b34aac131553c9f531b057661",
      "message": "Accept minute and hour units in ci-status --timeout\n\n--timeout 7200 meant to wait two hours was refused as over the 360-minute cap with no hint that the unit is minutes. Accept 90, 90m and 2h, and say how to write a value that looks like seconds.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-10T01:40:54Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "14cb85ddb451c56e7f29eb6125e067237050b75d",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/14cb85ddb451c56e7f29eb6125e067237050b75d",
      "message": "Name the missing install when a contrib build runs in a bare checkout\n\nA blueprint or package build in a worktree nobody installed failed deep in its first import with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND. Check for demo/node_modules first and point at contrib worktree setup. Packages that declare no dependencies still build without an install.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-10T01:40:53Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "cd530e3ceb37af7a9cb3ef6f0d595c967e0438c1",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/cd530e3ceb37af7a9cb3ef6f0d595c967e0438c1",
      "message": "Let contrib list options take every word up to the next option\n\nThe help already read --file PATH..., but --file a.test.ts b.test.ts silently dropped the second file into a positional slot. --file, --related and --exclude now collect each following word until the next option.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-10T01:40:53Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "7fcedff55a94cb1883050b4ab975466433636684",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/7fcedff55a94cb1883050b4ab975466433636684",
      "message": "Accept the workspace scope on unscoped package names in contrib\n\nHalf the demo packages are scoped (@al-ft/...) and half are not, so --package @al-ft/midgard-node was refused as unknown even though the workspace uses that scope. A directory name may now carry a scope the workspace declares; other scopes are still refused.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-10T01:40:53Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "ab02df92f35429cf952080ae4b26a2ffba10703d",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/ab02df92f35429cf952080ae4b26a2ffba10703d",
      "message": "Merge the Node CI fixes into the L1 follower integration",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-10T00:34:39Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "daad7a36790e3a2174a7d7f22944ba0bb6011753",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/daad7a36790e3a2174a7d7f22944ba0bb6011753",
      "message": "Keep the node's pure L1 modules pure and re-pin tests the follower lanes made stale\n\nThe retry-discipline change gave the pure event driver an import of the network transport package and a path to Math.random. The failure classification and hold now live in services/l1-follower.failure-hold.ts, and the driver takes it as a required option. The forced-order lint now excludes the database-reading own-landed-orphans module, next to its sibling read modules. The deployable-script counts drop by the 17 scripts of the retired native-script families and the deleted duplicate-event family. The merge maturity test mocks the poisoned-own-header read and gains a case for it. The startup CLI test expects the ruled behaviour: a deterministic failure holds the process unready, and an exhausted transient fails the command. Two test files over the line limit are split by topic.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-10T00:34:39Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "7fd4e3a509f42fd645a1d3d7eff56d70612ee0b3",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/7fd4e3a509f42fd645a1d3d7eff56d70612ee0b3",
      "message": "Merge the shift-grace invariant into the L1 follower integration",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-10T00:06:53Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "f747bb6696e67baf487cbc6260fc9fa4ed29d619",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/f747bb6696e67baf487cbc6260fc9fa4ed29d619",
      "message": "Require the new-shift inactivity grace to cover the maximum validity range\n\nA successor that inherits an event already overdue at its shift start needs up to the maximum validity range L to land the commit that covers it. With a 300 s grace and L = 480 s, an honest successor could be struck before that commit could land. Every profile now has to satisfy grace >= L, and all five set grace = L = 480 s. Only the scheduler spend script changes; fixtures, fit ledgers and the registry digest are regenerated for the new blueprint. The README also states that after a fraud removal, an event the removal re-exposes is held only to shift start + grace.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-10T00:06:49Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "c2f5ef8fbbf0f17b272d1c9319bcda1e278195d4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/c2f5ef8fbbf0f17b272d1c9319bcda1e278195d4",
      "message": "Merge colll78/l1-sfdfix into the L1 follower integration",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-09T23:41:04Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "34669d275d4bd9b649716e0d5ebd50040187b6a6",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/34669d275d4bd9b649716e0d5ebd50040187b6a6",
      "message": "Merge colll78/l1-tjfix into the L1 follower integration",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-09T23:41:04Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "26c3af4d2bd322b8c4974a39b5968c82ec88b2d7",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/26c3af4d2bd322b8c4974a39b5968c82ec88b2d7",
      "message": "Test the early side of the forced due window and drop citations of deleted predicates\n\nNo test exercised the early-window check of the forced-order fault, so weakening it went unnoticed. Three tests now pin inclusion at, before and just after the header start time. Comments that cited the deleted due predicate now cite the live rule.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-09T23:41:00Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "b1b022d8c9ffb07be98ad7ca44e34027099ffec0",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/b1b022d8c9ffb07be98ad7ca44e34027099ffec0",
      "message": "Treat ESRCH as a process that has exited when attesting a pid\n\nA process that exits between two /proc reads reports ESRCH on the second read. processIdentity threw on it, so liveness probes could fail on a dying pid and the lifecycle test raced in CI.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-09T23:41:00Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "5dba7c0b75952f42382bb96da17291007124d500",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/5dba7c0b75952f42382bb96da17291007124d500",
      "message": "Keep the commit-event depth out of fault-proof release identities\n\nThe commit-event depth that the depth work added to the manifest's L1 finality record leaked into the release policy that two fault-proofs producers record. The policy digest binds only the three rollback fields, so the first run passed. But a resumed workflow compared its recorded release identity against the watcher's three-field one, and recovery refused for good. Release policies are now projected to the digest-bound fields where they are made and where they are validated. The validation-dispute binding drops its private copy of the producer.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-09T23:41:00Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "e5a982a06d2af580957ad69347553aa91108cca0",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/e5a982a06d2af580957ad69347553aa91108cca0",
      "message": "Re-pin the module-size caps of the two tests edited after the strike merge",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-09T23:05:56Z"
    }
  ],
